From 26e6ff4fc7ccf85bff0db61baede31d1034be8db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincenzo Grimaldi <vince.ceccarelli@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 18:42:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0033 Phase C: every carry gate fails closed, proven by
 running (5481 passed)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Each item reproduces an INVENTORY finding, then refuses it. Tests first:
tests/test_carry_fail_closed.py, 36 new.

D8  No first leg without the pair gate AND one snapshot of the SAME marks.
    _open refuses PAIR_GATE_ABSENT / SNAPSHOT_ABSENT / SNAPSHOT_MISMATCH.
    Before: the gate ran only "if pair_risk is not None and snapshot is not
    None" — an engine built without either opened on the cost gates alone.

D7  borrow_apr has no default anywhere on the live path. CarryEngine(...,
    borrow_apr) and evaluate_entry(..., borrow_apr) require it;
    DEFAULT_BORROW_APR is deleted; config gains CARRY_BORROW_APR (a fraction
    in [0,1), None when absent) and build_bot REFUSES a carry book without
    it. Before: build_bot passed nothing and the engine financed at 5%.

D2  PAPER_TRADING now reaches the carry broker. CarryBroker requires an
    order_gate, asked before EVERY order: PAPER refuses; TESTNET may send;
    mainnet needs live authorisation AND promotion_gate_allows_live() — the
    broker asks again even though start() already refuses. An unreadable
    gate refuses. Run: USE_TESTNET=0 PAPER_TRADING=1 -> CarryOrderRefused,
    0 requests sent (was: a mainnet order body).

D4  A broken pair spends the day. CarryRisk.record_broken_pair() — same
    MAX_ENTRIES_PER_UTC_DAY, no new threshold. record_entry is still "both
    legs landed" only. Run: 10 ticks against a venue rejecting the perp ->
    2 spot orders (was 16).

F1  marketUnit=baseCoin on every spot market order. Without it Bybit reads a
    spot BUY qty as USDT. BybitClient always set it; CarryBroker did not.

D11 cumExecFee is carried per leg (LegFill.fee, Leg.fee). Unknown is None,
    never 0.0; an AST test forbids a literal zero fee in any carry module.
    Booking it is Phase E.

The engine still has no direction parameter (existing test, untouched).

TESTS CHANGED — each stricter, none weaker:
  test_carry_live_gates::test_the_gate_is_skipped_only_when_absent asserted
    that an engine WITHOUT a pair gate opens. That is the bypass. INVERTED:
    now test_an_absent_gate_is_a_refusal_not_a_skip — no gate, no leg.
  test_carry_costs::test_borrow_is_explicit_at_the_declaration pinned
    DEFAULT_BORROW_APR == 0.05, contradicting its own docstring. It now
    asserts there is no default at all.
  Fixtures, not assertions: test_carry_engine builds the engine the way
    main.tick drives it (pair gate + a snapshot stamped from each candle);
    16 evaluate_entry calls in test_carry_costs pass the 5% the default used
    to supply; carry configs pass CARRY_BORROW_APR; the broker helper passes
    an order gate. Every pre-existing assertion in those files is unchanged.

